ht="56"><span class="enc-name">Scanian War</span><span class="enc-type">War · 1675–1679</span><span class="enc-snip">The Scanian War was fought from 1675 to 1679 between Denmark-Norway and Sweden, as part of the wider Franco-Dutch War.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/scarborough-fair"><span class="enc-name">Scarborough Fair</span><span class="enc-type">Work / monument</span><span class="enc-snip">&quot;Scarborough Fair&quot; (Roud 12, Child 2) is a traditional ballad of northern England.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/scarborough-tobago"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/scarborough-tobago.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Scarborough, Tobago</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Scarborough is the capital and main port of Tobago, in Trinidad and Tobago, on the island's southern coast.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/scarpetta-ordelaffi"><span class="enc-name">Scarpetta Ordelaffi</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Scarpetta Ordelaffi was lord of Forlì in Romagna at the start of the 14th century and a leader of the region's Ghibellines.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/scattery-island"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/scattery-island.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Scattery Island</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Scattery Island is a small island in the Shannon estuary off Kilrush, County Clare, Ireland.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/scetis"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/scetis.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Scetis</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Scetis, the Wadi el-Natrun in the desert west of the Nile Delta in Egypt, was one of the main centres of early Christian monasticism.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/schaan"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/schaan.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Schaan</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Schaan is the largest municipality of Liechtenstein, just north of the capital Vaduz on the Rhine plain.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/schalksburg"><span class="enc-name">Schalksburg</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">The Schalksburg was a castle on a hill near Balingen and Albstadt in the Swabian Jura, in Baden-Württemberg, Germany.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/schanfigg"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/schanfigg.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Schanfigg</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">The Schanfigg is a valley in the Swiss canton of Graubünden, running from Chur up the Plessur river to the resort of Arosa.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/scheduled-castes"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/scheduled-castes.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Scheduled Castes</span><span class="enc-type">People / group</span><span class="enc-snip">Scheduled Castes is the official term in India for the communities historically subjected to untouchability, listed in a schedule under the constitution.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/scheduled-tribes"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/scheduled-tribes.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Scheduled Tribes</span><span class="enc-type">People / group</span><span class="enc-snip">Scheduled Tribes is the official designation in India for indigenous communities, often called Adivasis, listed under the constitution of 1950.</span></a></li></ul>
